L4-E4: BOARD A'S CURRENT-LIMIT COORDINATION (U3 IIN_HOST, R11) AND THE OUTLET'S TRIP (R138) (l4e4_limits.py,
MESHSAT-1357; second round, after check astra-check-l4e4-1). PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing bought, built, powered or
measured; no generator, registry or page edited.
Basis per figure: MAKER (document, page), NETLIST, MODELED, INFERRED (method stated), ASSUMPTION; INCONCLUSIVE where no
held document gives the figure.

0. REPRODUCTIONS (refused, exit 4, if either fails)
   0a r11_dep.py re-run in a child process reproduces r11_dep.out byte for byte (sha256/16 f9d2c6f23fab3edc): yes
   0b r11_dep.main() run in this process, its locals taken at return, prints the same bytes: yes. Taken from that run:
      VSNS, the ISNS offset, the TCR, U3's accuracy, the other loads, the temperatures, the stage relations, band(),
      lcsc_fill.py's map and the C2903468 reading. The TOLERANCE is read, not typed: the HoJLR2512 sheet p.1 'F=±1%'
      and each part's LCSC answer (±1% for C2903468, the chosen R11 and R138); r11_dep.py's band(), which types 1 %
      inside, is checked to equal the band at the read tolerance (exit 4 otherwise)
   pinned: r11_dep.py 6636a7489d3d1406, l4e_replay.out 59c6eeab16da98f8; board A's netlist sha256/16 6c40250c47195ebb (r11_dep.py's 14 facts hold on it)

1. U3's IIN_HOST FOR REQ-016's 100 W WINDOW, R16 INCLUDED (check B1)
   U3 regulates the voltage across its RAC, R16 '10mOhm 1% 2512 (RAC, input current sense)' (NETLIST), lcsc_fill.py's C2903468 HoJLR2512-3W-10mR-1% (the same
     HoJLR2512 series: ±1%, TCR 50 ppm/K, MAKER p.1 and p.2). Its bounds in board current are U3's own bounds divided by
     R16's factor. R16's temperature: r11_dep.py's envelope, -20 C to the ASSUMED 100 C (75 K from 25 C); no thermal figure
     is held for R16 either. R16 at its lowest: x0.98629 (U3 passes the most); at its highest: x1.01379 (the least)
   board current: maximum = U3's maximum (the larger of SLUSE66A p.80's 100 mA and p.1's +-2.5 %) / R16 low; minimum =
     (setting less the records' INFERRED 0.10 A, C-7, conditional) / R16 high; through R11 the maximum plus C-9's 0.079094 A
   what the window needs at VBUS20 (MODELED, l4e_replay.out 8; the lowest bus 19.146 V) and the setting that covers it:
     declared     0.93 x 0.93: 86.5 W, at least 4.517 A: setting 4.70 A (minimum 4.537 A, maximum 4.884 A, through R11 4.964 A)
                                     the first round's 4.65 A with R16 in: minimum 4.488 A (-0.029 A), through R11 4.912 A
     high bracket 0.97 x 0.97: 94.1 W, at least 4.914 A: setting 5.10 A (minimum 4.932 A, maximum 5.300 A, through R11 5.379 A)
                                     the first round's 5.05 A with R16 in: minimum 4.883 A (-0.031 A), through R11 5.327 A
     no loss      1.00 x 1.00: 100.0 W, at least 5.223 A: setting 5.40 A (minimum 5.228 A, maximum 5.612 A, through R11 5.691 A)
                                     the first round's 5.35 A with R16 in: minimum 5.179 A (-0.044 A), through R11 5.639 A
   CHOSEN: IIN_HOST 4.70 A. The first round's 4.65 A fails with R16 in: its minimum 4.488 A is under the 4.517 A the window
     needs, and its 4.912 A through R11 exceeds the first round's hot full-tap minimum (section 2). 4.70 A is the smallest
     50 mA code whose minimum covers the need: 4.537 A, +0.020 A. Evidence for the declared row: the declared efficiencies are
     the only ones this tree holds (C-8 open). The corrected path's result is unchanged (MODELED, l4e_replay.out 8: A2
     window-sized 286.3 / 516.5 Wh unserved at 48 / 72 h, as at the drafted 6.2 A's 286.3 / 516.5 Wh): any limit at or above the need
     carries all the window gives (INFERRED from that equality). U3's maximum above the need is A-2's collapse case, handled
     by A-2's rule (item 1), as for any setting
   REGISTER (MAKER SLUSE66A p.80, 9.6.22 and Figure 9-35): RSNS_RAC = 0b for the 10 mOhm R16 (p.25, 9.3.5, 'if 10-mOhm
     sensing is used please configure RSNS_RAC=0b'; the POR default is 5 mOhm); range 50 to 6350 mA, 50 mA resolution, a
     7-bit code in bits 14:8: code 94 (0x5E), REG0x0F/0E() = 0x5E00; U3's own maximum 4.817 A (nominal + 100 mA = 4.800 A,
     +2.5 % = 4.817 A), in board current 4.884 A. Rewritten after every adapter removal, which resets IIN_HOST to 3.25 A
     (p.26, 9.3.6): A-2's startup rule
   TI's accuracy (MAKER SLUSE66A): p.1 '+-2.5 % input current regulation' (a feature line, no conditions); p.10, 8.5
     Electrical Characteristics, IIN_DPM_REG_ACC over -40 to 105 C, rows only for the 5 mOhm RAC: 7.8 A: 7.6 to 8.0 A; 5.8 A: 5.6 to 6.0 A; 2.8 A: 2.6 to 3.0 A; 0.8 A: 0.6 to 1.0 A
     (+-0.2 A, +-1 mV of sense voltage); no row for the 10 mOhm RAC; neither includes the external resistor's tolerance
