5. INCONCLUSIVE, AND WHAT THE BENCH MUST STILL SHOW
   INCONCLUSIVE: C-7 (U3's minimum for the 10 mOhm RAC; the setting is CONDITIONAL on the INFERRED 0.10 A); J_USBC_OUT's pin
     rating (no part); which VI(TRIP) row the strap selects (the maker's label conflict; bench (a) decides it); R11's and
     R16's actual temperatures (the 100 C stays an ASSUMPTION; the rise is the derating line's); the efficiencies (C-8)
   bench 7b.1: the front end's CC onset with an electronic load past U3, at -20, 25 and 62 C: above 4.964 A at each
   bench 7b.3: R11's Kelvin error, at most 0.38 mOhm x I at 25 C (1.89 mV at 4.964 A)
   C-7: at the 4.70 A setting, the input current by a reference meter at or above 4.60 A x 10 mOhm / R16 measured four-wire
     (at least 4.537 A over R16's envelope), and at or above the window's 4.517 A
   the outlet: bench (a) and (b) of section 3

